course: dictionary
lesson: 15644
title: Thai: from a place, a person, a language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Thai» tells us where something comes from. Thailand is a country in Southeast Asia, so Thai food, Thai music and Thai temples all belong to Thailand. Thai is an adjective here, and it always starts with a capital letter.
explain: Look at this sentence: «Mia ate Thai green curry for dinner.» Thai tells us which curry it was. Try swapping in another country, like «Italian green curry», and the sentence still makes sense, so Thai is describing the curry.
explain: Thai can also be a noun. «Two Thais came to our school today» means two people from Thailand. Thai can be a language too: «She speaks Thai at home.» Read the words around it to see which meaning is being used.
fact: Thailand is a country in Southeast Asia. Its capital city is Bangkok.
fact: A Thai is a person from Thailand. The plural is Thais.
fact: Thai is the main language of Thailand. It has its own alphabet.
fact: Thai has five tones, so the same sound can mean different things when your voice goes up, down or stays flat.
fact: Thailand was once called Siam, and its national animal is the elephant.
exercise: «Mia ate Thai green curry for dinner.» What does Thai tell us about the curry? | It is always served cold | It was made by a robot | *It comes from Thailand | It is a kind of dessert
exercise: «Two Thais came to our school today.» What is a Thai in this sentence? | A kind of noodle | A city in Asia | A type of elephant | *A person from Thailand
exercise: Which city is the capital of Thailand? | Siam | Phuket | Chiang Mai | *Bangkok
test: «She speaks Thai at home.» What is Thai in this sentence? | A person from Thailand | A green curry | A festival | *The language
test: Which Thai festival is famous for a huge water fight? | Christmas | Bonfire Night | Halloween | *Songkran
exam: Which phrase uses Thai to describe a thing? | *Thai boxing | She learned Thai | Two Thais came | He is from Thai
